$DATUM (R)-6-((3R,4R)-1,3-Dimethyl-piperidin-4-yl)-7-(2-fluoro-4-methyl-phenyl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
hydrochloride acid (17k). To a mixture of
(R)-7-bromo-6-((3R,4R)-1,3-dimethyl-piperidin-4-yl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4atriaza-phenanthren-3-one
(intermediate obtained at Step B during preparation of compound 17l, 1.25
g, 3.07 mmol), (2-fluoro-4-methylphenyl)boronic acid (0.52 g, 3.38 mmol),
potassium carbonate (0.848 g, 6.16 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (12 mL) and water
(2 mL) was added PdCl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2 adduct (0.251 g, 0.307 mmol) and the
reaction mixture was heated at 90 °C overnight. The reaction mixture was
cooled to ambient temperature and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (eluting with 0-20% MeOH
in DCM).
(R)-6-((3R,4R)-1,3-dimethyl-piperidin-4-yl)-7-(2-fluoro-4-methyl-phenyl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
(1.08 g, 81%) as a yellow solid. The product was treated with HCl (4M in
EtOAc, 10 mL) and stirred at ambient temperature for 0.5 h. The mixture
was concentrated in vacuo and the residue was re-crystallized from 15%
DCM in EtOAc.
(R)-6-((3R,4R)-1,3-dimethyl-piperidin-4-yl)-7-(2-fluoro-4-methyl-phenyl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triazaphenanthren-3-one
hydrochloride (compound 17k, 1.003 g, 86%). Crude product: 1H NMR (400
MHz, CD3OD): δ 7.11-6.99 (m, 3H), 6.93 (s, 1H), 6.77 (s, 1H), 4.90-4.94
(m, 1H), 4.64-4.56 (m, 2H), 2.99-2.97 (m, 1H), 2.80 (m, 2H), 2.63-2.60
(m, 1H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 2.30-2.24 (m, 1H), 2.18 (s, 3H), 1.98-1.95 (m,
1H), 1.87-1.85 (m, 1H), 1.59-1.56 (m, 2H), 1.48 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.82
(d, J=7.2 Hz, 3H). LC/MS (Table 1, Method 7) Rt = 0.746 min; MS (ESI):
m/z 437 [M+H]+. Recrystallized product: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ
7.16-7.12 (m, 1H), 7.09-7.02 (m, 1H), 6.90 (s, 1H), 6.82 (s, 1H),
4.92-4.91 (m, 1H), 4.66-4.58 (m, 2H), 3.58 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1H),
3.31-3.24 (m, 1H), 3.06-3.03 (m, 2H), 2.93-2.87 (m, 1H), 2.80 (s, 3H),
2.53-2.50 (m, 1H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 1.91 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 2H), 1.48 (d, J =
6.4 Hz, 3H), 0.91 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H). LC/MS (Table 1, Method 4) Rt =
1.769 min; MS (ESI): m/z 437 [M+H]+. SFC (Table 4, Method 5), Rt = 3.120
min.
